{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/248926-troupe-roleplaying-inspiration-from-ars-magica","id":248926,"title":"Troupe Roleplaying: Inspiration from Ars Magica","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-04T09:52:28-07:00","id":248926,"title":"Troupe Roleplaying: Inspiration from Ars Magica","content":"Idly thinking about Werewolf's Pack structure. I realized that the hunting party/wolf-blooded/regular mortals paradigm pretty accurately parallels the mages/companions/grogs structure from Ars Magica. Which then got me thinking about troupe gaming and how it seems particularly useful for Werewolf: The Forsaken.<br /> <br /> I know that I'm just trying to make this work so that I can actually play this game instead of always running it. Which is why I've come here to try and work out my ideas. The biggest hurdle I'm running into is &quot;Why wouldn't the entire hunting party stay together?&quot; In Ars Magica, magical research is measured in a range of months, so if a mage doesn't want to take part in an adventure, they have a good reason.<br /> <br /> Since I don't like coming into these things empty-handed, here are the solutions I've come up with so far:<ul><li>Loose pack organization. If it's spread out over an area, and generally not well-patrolled, you end up having a good reason why a pack member simply wouldn't be around: they're off doing their own thing in the next county.</li> <li>Large pack. Large enough to support multiple hunting parties. This could also be something like a pack coalition, or you've got a patron character like Max Roman who can convince neighbouring packs to send help now and again.</li> <li>Captured! If you've got a player who ST's very infrequently, the natural explanation is that their character got captured and/or incapacitated. Comes with a built-in adventure hook.</li> </ul><br /> Have any of y'all tried this before with your werewolf games? How did it work? Is this a fool's hope?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T21:26:01-07:00","id":249455,"title":"","content":"Well, one thing I've tried is giving all the Hunting Party members (that is, PCs) their own personal lives and personal things to do. That way, it's easier to explain away a disappearance due to non-attendance. Anyone could be patrolling the territory at any time, and running into trouble (or something interesting), especially in the Spirit Wilds. Or, they could just be doing their own thing; the Blood Talons attending an NPC's initiation in a neighboring territory (all Suthar Anzuth love getting their gaba'al on, after all), the Ithaeur could be learning Rites someplace, the Cahalith swim team coach was called away to attend a conference, etc.<br /> <br /> The only time, in my experience, that this could not work is during in-game circumstances when the Pack SHOULD be sticking together, e.g. they are currently at war vs. not one, but TWO Pure Packs, plus give or take a swarm of Beshilu and a minor Incarna of anti-Industry. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T04:58:35-07:00","id":249702,"title":"","content":"That's an elegant idea that I hadn't considered. I tend to get tunnel vision as a ST.<br /> <br /> And I dunno, if you're fighting a war on 4+ fronts, splitting up seems like it would be a necessity. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> By the way, all that jargon in your first paragraph is why I'm terrified to run this game for my group. Though &quot;Suthar Anzuth love getting their gaba'al on&quot; has to be the best sentence I've heard all week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T09:58:15-07:00","id":249894,"title":"","content":"Well, it wasn't necessarily a 4-front war. What happened in my game was that the 2 Pure packs were allied; one was the alpha pack who ordered the massacre of all Forsaken packs in the PCs' territory, while the other (hmmm, was there actually 3 Pure packs? I cannot remember now, lol) was the beta pack who were basically &quot;The Army.&quot; The Beshilu were driven into the territory by the Fire-Touched pack as a prelude to war, to sow chaos and thin out the Urdaga's resources. The lesser incarna of Anti-Industry, was a long-term enemy of the pack, and not part of the war.<br /> <br /> Also, sorry about the first paragraph, although I am one of those who share the sentiment that the in-setting jargon KICKS ASS, particularly because of the imagery and emotions they tend to evoke, and I've been reading/STing Werewolf on and off ever since 2007 or so, so it comes as second-nature to me. I'm sure that with experience, though, you'll be able to do the same. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T10:52:20-07:00","id":249944,"title":"","content":"I'm good with the jargon myself (still occasionally mix up <i>urhan</i> and <i>urshul</i>) it's just that my players aren't, and I know it's going to be an uphill battle using it in-game. I'm half-tempted to do a Tier 1 &quot;Learn how to Werewolf&quot; chronicle leading up to the actual game just to make sure they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T14:50:56-07:00","id":250148,"title":"","content":"Reading Mr Shopping's &quot;The Ties That Bind&quot; and, later on, &quot;Detroit Rock City&quot; (look up the Actual Plays on RPG.net, if interested) is how I learned to incorporate First Tongue into common slang, especially where urban Uratha are involved. This is probably a hit-or-miss thing, though, depending on your players; I may have a knack for language and wordplay, but most people don't share that trait, especially if it's only for game immersion's sake.<br /> <br /> As the ST, however, YOU have the power to breathe the life that you want into your game, though of course with certain limits. Make NPC wolves that awe the players (awe, but not outshine; there's always a balance to be struck), who speak the First Tongue like they'd been born with it. Make up local color; I'm sure werewolves of a particular area have their own naming conventions, forms of praise and forms of insult, stories that they share during ungin (inter-pack meetings), tribal/pack initiation rites, etc.<br /> <br /> Of course, your players might not always appreciate or even catch on to the amount of detail you've put into the game, but that's alright; everyone's dim from time to time, and we all need to learn a little more patience (ESPECIALLY those of us who can turn into towering monstrosities of RAGE and RAAAGH!). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think about 50% of my STing efforts goes into writing up background stuff for my games. The setting, whether small town or developing industrial city, has its background story; I dream up of a whole bunch of little places of interest, each of which have their own stories as well. NPCs have stories depending on whether I feel like it or not, although its more often that I do feel like it. It doesn't matter whether my players discover these little details or not, although of course it feels great when they do, and when they appreciate them. The effort is more for MY benefit as ST; I don't have to spend so much time coming up with grandiose plots to involve my PCs in, when can they can make epic plots happen on their own simply by crashing headlong against my verisimilitude. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, good luck with your game, mate. Looking forward to seeing how it goes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}